From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: keep the external shell's HALFTONE mapping under clipping

Purpose: draw the same pixels for a stretched image whether it is painted
whole or in parts.
Wine before: a clipped StretchBlt or StretchDIBits with HALFTONE recomputed
the scale for the clipped rectangle and dropped the neighbouring source
pixel, so a partial repaint of a Luna caption changed its colours.
Change: keep the original stretch coordinates and phase, and keep the
neighbouring source sample that bilinear interpolation needs; both
functions use the same visibility rule.
Evidence: tests/halftone-clip.c (1408 cases of formats, stretch directions,
mirroring, clips and viewports); Luna's caption keeps its pixels under
partial WM_PAINT updates.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
Old patches: 0036.
---
 dlls/win32u/bitblt.c            |  12 ++-
 dlls/win32u/dib.c               |   2 +-
 dlls/win32u/dibdrv/primitives.c | 205 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 dlls/win32u/ntgdi_private.h     |   2 +-
 4 files changed, 133 insertions(+), 88 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/bitblt.c b/dlls/win32u/bitblt.c
index 7721d3b..95e6246 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/bitblt.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/bitblt.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
